MID_SE_Lor_Sar_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_C_001: Damn... I don't recognize any of this.
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_C_002: Is that Loretta? Is she lost?
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_C_003: I'd feel bad if I pretended not to see her...
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_C_004: Hi there, Loretta. Do you need help?
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_C_005: Sha Lan! Everything's good. I'm good.
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_C_006: You were looking around nervously, so I thought you\nwere lost.
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_C_007: Nope! I was just...checking out the neighborhood.
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_C_008: I see. Well, that's probably enough exploring. Let's\ngo home.
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_C_009: The people at your temple will worry if you're out\nso late. Do you want to hold my hand?
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_C_010: No! I'm not some kid who needs to hold on to\nmommy. Get lost, will you?
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_C_011: That's not the right way. You're going in the opposite\ndirection of home.
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_C_012: Yeah, I know! I don't need your help.
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_C_013: Come with me. Once it gets dark, there could be\nrobberies, kidnappings...that sort of thing.
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_C_014: I ain't scared. In fact, I'd be right at home sleeping\nin an alley around here.
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_C_015: No. A young girl like you shouldn't do that.
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_C_016: Yeah, people like you from good homes tend to\nsay that stuff.
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_C_017: I'm used to it, but you? You probably have no idea\nwhat it's like to live on the streets.
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_C_018: That's true. I've never lived on the streets of a city\nwith this many people.
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_C_019: Though I don't think my home was as good as\nyou imagine. I was hungry all the time.
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_C_020: What are you mumbling about? Listen, quit trying\nso hard to help.
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_C_021: Alright, then. If you insist, I'll leave you on your own.
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_C_022: Huh? Y-yeah, that's what I'm saying.
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_C_023: Besides, I don't have the time to be with someone\nwho is choosing to put herself in danger.
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_C_024: To be honest, I don't want anything to do with the\ntemples. Sorry for bothering you. See you.
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_C_025: Sure...
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_C_026: Wait, did she seriously leave?! Damn it! What was I\nbeing so stubborn for?!
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_B_001: Hi, Loretta. Did you need something?
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_B_002: Ugh, you noticed. I must be getting rusty at sneaking\nup on people.
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_B_003: Were you following me? What are you up to? Are the\ntemples behind this?
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_B_004: I was watching you in case you got in some\nkinda trouble.
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_B_005: I thought maybe I could swoop in and help you out\nof a jam, to turn the tables.
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_B_006: Well, how kind of you. And that's the only reason?
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_B_007: If you don't like me, it makes more sense to stay\naway from me.
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_B_008: I figure you're still mad at me for leaving you alone\nthat one time.
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_B_009: Nah. That's not it. I actually, uh, wanted to tell\nyou something.
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_B_010: I'm really sorry! Also, thanks!
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_B_011: Hang on—why?
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_B_012: Last time you tried to help me, I was kind of a\nbrat about it.
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_B_013: You are surprisingly sincere. I thought you were\ngoing to grouse at me again.
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_B_014: I dunno why I got so defensive. I thought about it\nlater and felt pretty bad.
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_B_015: You were worried about me, and I kept throwing\nit back in your face.
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_B_016: Hey, it's OK. I'm the one who should apologize\nfor leaving you behind. I'm sorry.
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_B_017: I was a bit harsh because you're from the temples.
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_B_018: Don't sweat it. We're good!
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_B_019: I was curious, though—how come you seem so\nat home here?
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_B_020: Aren't you from the middle of nowhere? People\nlike you always get lost in the big city.
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_B_021: Heh, because you never get lost, right?
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_B_022: You got it all wrong. I was just late getting home...
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_B_023: I did get lost here in the city initially, but I find my\nway around fine now.
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_B_024: If you don't adapt quickly to your environment, it's\nhard to survive.
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_B_025: Back home, it was normal to go without meals for\ndays. If you got lost outside the village, you'd starve.
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_B_026: Kids like you didn't last long in Kunlun.
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_B_027: Ha, just pulling your leg.
MID_SE_Lor_Sar_B_028: Note to self...never visit the middle of nowhere.